event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":602,"item_id":"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3c9ce3d8819185c363cb9888f4fa","output_index":0,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":20,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/inputs\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M003\\\",\\\"M004\\\",\\\"M005\\\",\\\"M006\\\",\\\"M007\\\",\\\"M008\\\",\\\"M009\\\",\\\"N001\\\",\\\"N002\\\",\\\"N003\\\",\\\"N004\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/0/uses\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M004\\\",\\\"M005\\\",\\\"M006\\\",\\\"N001\\\",\\\"N002\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"Fix r>0, J=[r/2,3r/2], and choose compact C from H003. For every s∈J, u(·,s)=q off C. Smoothness implies derivatives vanish there, so e and e_t are continuous and supported in C. M001 applies to e, giving integrability and making E the ordinary finite integral. C×J is compact by M005; M004 gives uniform continuity of e_t on it. Applying M006 with F(τ)(x)=e(x,τ) and F′(τ)(x)=e_t(x,τ), the compact support, measurability, integrable base function, integrable majorant, and pointwise derivative conditions established here give E′(r)=∫e_t. The independently exported N001 and N002 state these support/integrability and differentiation conclusions for every positive time.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/uses\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M003\\\",\\\"M007\\\",\\\"N003\\\",\\\"N004\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"For each j set g_j=u_t·u_{x_j}. Its spatial derivative is continuous and compactly supported, so M001 gives integrability. Apply M007 on each coordinate line with second factor 1; the endpoint values of g_j vanish, hence ∫∂_j g_j=0. Product integrability and S-finiteness permit M003 to identify the whole-space integral with the iterated line integral. Expanding ∂_j g_j and summing gives E′(r)=2∫u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu), precisely N003. Differentiating H001 yields u·u_t=0; H002 gives u_{tt}−Δ_xu=a u, so the integrand vanishes pointwise, as exported in N004. Therefore E′(r)=0. The Euclidean vector dot products and Frobenius sum have exactly the stated componentwise meanings, and no regularity of a is used.\\\"}]}\"}"}

